{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Embedded Feature Selection Model.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Embedded Feature Selection Model.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"embedded feature selection model embedded feature selection model","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Embedded Feature Selection Model.md","fileName":"Embedded Feature Selection Model.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Embedded Feature Selection Model","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 21:00\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Classification Feature Selection]] · [[Advanced Feature Selection]] · [[Big Data Preprocessing]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Classification Feature Selection","Advanced Feature Selection","Big Data Preprocessing","dataclassification.pdf","featureengineeringformachinelearninganddataanalytics.pdf","frontiersofdatascience.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Embedded Feature Selection Model.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Embedded Feature Selection Model.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"embedded feature selection model embedded feature selection model","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Embedded Feature Selection Model.md","fileName":"Embedded Feature Selection Model.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Embedded Feature Selection Model","heading":"Embedded Feature Selection Model","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"An embedded feature selection model chooses variables as part of classifier fitting rather than as a separate preprocessing search. The selection decision and estimation of predictive parameters occur together.\n\nThe source presents embedded selection as a bridge between fast filter scoring and accurate wrapper evaluation. Sparse penalties and tree split selection are typical mechanisms through which a learning objective can suppress unnecessary variables while fitting the model.\n\nEmbedded methods can exploit the learning algorithm's internal structure while avoiding a separate wrapper search. The selected subset is consequently tied to the model objective, regularization, and fitting procedure.\n\nThat integration can be computationally favorable for large datasets because selection occurs during a fit that was already required. Scalability still depends on whether the learning algorithm itself can be distributed or adapted to streaming data.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Classification Feature Selection","Advanced Feature Selection","Big Data Preprocessing","dataclassification.pdf","featureengineeringformachinelearninganddataanalytics.pdf","frontiersofdatascience.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Embedded Feature Selection Model.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Embedded Feature Selection Model.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"embedded feature selection model embedded feature selection model","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Embedded Feature Selection Model.md","fileName":"Embedded Feature Selection Model.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Embedded Feature Selection Model","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[dataclassification.pdf]]\n\n[[featureengineeringformachinelearninganddataanalytics.pdf]]\n\n[[frontiersofdatascience.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Classification Feature Selection","Advanced Feature Selection","Big Data Preprocessing","dataclassification.pdf","featureengineeringformachinelearninganddataanalytics.pdf","frontiersofdatascience.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}